-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering of the Delaware Code Online, not the
-- official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- The text treats "an electronic transmission" as a defined term elsewhere (section 232(d), piece dg5); here the
-- fact that a document is an electronic transmission is a plain input.

§ `Section 116 -- Document form, signature and delivery`

§§ `s 116(a)(1) Documents`

-- src:222 | (a) Except as provided in subsection (b) of this section, without limiting the manner in which any act or transaction may be documented, or the manner in which a document may be signed or delivered:
-- src:223 | Any act or transaction contemplated or governed by this chapter or the certificate of incorporation or bylaws may be provided for in a document, and an electronic transmission shall be deemed the equivalent of a written …
-- src:224 | a. Any tangible medium on which information is inscribed, and includes handwritten, typed, printed or similar instruments, and copies of such instruments; and
-- src:225 | b. An electronic transmission.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(a)(1) (src:222-225)
DECLARE `s 116(a)(1) Medium` IS ONE OF
    `a tangible medium on which information is inscribed, including handwritten, typed, printed or similar instruments, and copies of such instruments`
    `an electronic transmission`
    `another medium`

-- "Document" means a tangible medium on which information is inscribed (including handwritten, typed, printed or
-- similar instruments, and copies) or an electronic transmission. The definition is closed ("means").
-- src:223 | “Document” means:
-- src:224 | a. Any tangible medium on which information is inscribed, and includes handwritten, typed, printed or similar instruments, and copies of such instruments; and
-- src:225 | b. An electronic transmission.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(a)(1) (src:223-225)
GIVEN medium IS A `s 116(a)(1) Medium`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 116(a)(1) the medium is a document` medium MEANS
    CONSIDER medium
    WHEN `a tangible medium on which information is inscribed, including handwritten, typed, printed or similar instruments, and copies of such instruments` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an electronic transmission` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another medium` THEN FALSE

-- Any act or transaction contemplated or governed by this chapter, the certificate or the bylaws may be provided for
-- in a document, and an electronic transmission is deemed the equivalent of a written document.
-- src:223 | Any act or transaction contemplated or governed by this chapter or the certificate of incorporation or bylaws may be provided for in a document, and an electronic transmission shall be deemed the equivalent of a written …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(a)(1) (src:223)
GIVEN medium IS A `s 116(a)(1) Medium`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 116(a)(1) the medium is deemed the equivalent of a written document` medium MEANS
    CONSIDER medium
    WHEN `a tangible medium on which information is inscribed, including handwritten, typed, printed or similar instruments, and copies of such instruments` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an electronic transmission` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another medium` THEN FALSE

§§ `s 116(a)(2) Signatures`

-- src:226 | (2) Whenever this chapter or the certificate of incorporation or bylaws requires or permits a signature, the signature may be a manual, facsimile, conformed or electronic signature. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(a)(2) (src:226)
DECLARE `s 116(a)(2) Form of signature` IS ONE OF
    `a manual signature`
    `a facsimile signature`
    `a conformed signature`
    `an electronic signature`
    `another form of signature`

-- Whenever the chapter, the certificate or the bylaws require or permit a signature, it may be a manual, facsimile,
-- conformed or electronic signature. Another form is not covered (NOTHING).
-- src:226 | (2) Whenever this chapter or the certificate of incorporation or bylaws requires or permits a signature, the signature may be a manual, facsimile, conformed or electronic signature. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(a)(2) (src:226)
GIVEN form IS A `s 116(a)(2) Form of signature`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(a)(2) the form of signature may be used` form MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `a manual signature` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a facsimile signature` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a conformed signature` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an electronic signature` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another form of signature` THEN NOTHING

-- "Electronic signature" means an electronic symbol or process that is attached to, or logically associated with, a
-- document and executed or adopted by a person with an intent to execute, authenticate or adopt the document.
-- src:226 | “Electronic signature” means an electronic symbol or process that is attached to, or logically associated with, a document and executed or adopted by a person with an intent to execute, authenticate or adopt the document. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(a)(2) (src:226)
GIVEN `the symbol or process is electronic` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is attached to, or logically associated with, a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is executed or adopted by a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has an intent to execute, authenticate or adopt the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 116(a)(2) the symbol or process is an electronic signature` `the symbol or process is electronic` `it is attached to, or logically associated with, a document` `it is executed or adopted by a person` `the person has an intent to execute, authenticate or adopt the document` MEANS
        `the symbol or process is electronic`
    AND `it is attached to, or logically associated with, a document`
    AND `it is executed or adopted by a person`
    AND `the person has an intent to execute, authenticate or adopt the document`

-- src:226 | A person may execute a document with such person’s signature.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(a)(2) (src:226)
GIVEN `the person's signature is a signature the person has made or adopted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 116(a)(2) the person may execute a document with the person's signature` `the person's signature is a signature the person has made or adopted` MEANS
    `the person's signature is a signature the person has made or adopted`

§§ `s 116(a)(3) Delivery of an electronic transmission`

-- Unless otherwise agreed between the sender and recipient (and, for proxies or consents given by or on behalf of a
-- stockholder, subject to the additional requirements of section 212(c)(2) and (3) (piece dg4) and 228(d)(1) (piece
-- dg5)), an electronic transmission is deemed delivered when it enters an information processing system that the
-- person has designated for receiving electronic transmissions of the type delivered, so long as it is in a form
-- capable of being processed by that system and the person is able to retrieve it. If the sender and recipient agreed
-- otherwise, the agreement governs (NOTHING).
-- src:227 | (3) Unless otherwise agreed between the sender and recipient (and in the case of proxies or consents given by or on behalf of a stockholder, subject to the additional requirements set forth in § 212(c)(2) and (3) and § 228(d)(1) of this title, respectively), an electronic transmission shall be deemed delivered to a person for purposes of this chapter and the certificate of incorporation and bylaws when it enters an information processing system that the person has designated for the purpose of receiving electronic transmissions of the type delivered, so long as the electronic transmission is in a form capable of being processed by that system and such person is able to retrieve the electronic transmission. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(a)(3) (src:227)
GIVEN `the sender and recipient have agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transmission has entered an information processing system that the person has designated for the purpose of receiving electronic transmissions of the type delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transmission is in a form capable of being processed by that system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is able to retrieve the transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transmission is a proxy or consent given by or on behalf of a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the additional requirements of § 212(c)(2) and (3) or § 228(d)(1) are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(a)(3) the electronic transmission is deemed delivered to the person` `the sender and recipient have agreed otherwise` `the transmission has entered an information processing system that the person has designated for the purpose of receiving electronic transmissions of the type delivered` `the transmission is in a form capable of being processed by that system` `the person is able to retrieve the transmission` `the transmission is a proxy or consent given by or on behalf of a stockholder` `the additional requirements of § 212(c)(2) and (3) or § 228(d)(1) are met` MEANS
    -- out of range: sections 212(c)(2) and (3) (piece dg4) and 228(d)(1) (piece dg5)
    IF `the sender and recipient have agreed otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    `the transmission has entered an information processing system that the person has designated for the purpose of receiving electronic transmissions of the type delivered`
               AND `the transmission is in a form capable of being processed by that system`
               AND `the person is able to retrieve the transmission`
               AND (   (NOT (`the transmission is a proxy or consent given by or on behalf of a stockholder`))
                    OR `the additional requirements of § 212(c)(2) and (3) or § 228(d)(1) are met`))

-- Whether a person has so designated a system is determined by the certificate, the bylaws, or the context and
-- surrounding circumstances, including the parties' conduct.
-- src:227 | Whether a person has so designated an information processing system is determined by the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws or from the context and surrounding circumstances, including the parties’ …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(a)(3) (src:227)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws show that the person designated the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context and surrounding circumstances, including the parties' conduct, show that the person designated the system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 116(a)(3) the person has designated the information processing system` `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws show that the person designated the system` `the context and surrounding circumstances, including the parties' conduct, show that the person designated the system` MEANS
        `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws show that the person designated the system`
     OR `the context and surrounding circumstances, including the parties' conduct, show that the person designated the system`

-- An electronic transmission is delivered under the section even if no person is aware of its receipt.
-- src:227 | An electronic transmission is delivered under this section even if no person is aware of its …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(a)(3) (src:227)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 116(a)(3) delivery requires that a person be aware of the receipt` MEANS FALSE

-- Receipt of an electronic acknowledgement from an information processing system establishes that the electronic
-- transmission was received but, by itself, does not establish that the content sent corresponds to the content
-- received.
-- src:227 | Receipt of an electronic acknowledgement from an information processing system establishes that an electronic transmission was received but, by itself, does not establish that the content sent corresponds to the content received.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(a)(3) (src:227)
GIVEN `an electronic acknowledgement was received from the information processing system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 116(a)(3) the electronic acknowledgement establishes that the electronic transmission was received` `an electronic acknowledgement was received from the information processing system` MEANS
    `an electronic acknowledgement was received from the information processing system`

-- src:227 | Receipt of an electronic acknowledgement from an information processing system establishes that an electronic transmission was received but, by itself, does not establish that the content sent corresponds to the content received.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(a)(3) (src:227)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 116(a)(3) the electronic acknowledgement by itself establishes that the content sent corresponds to the content received` MEANS FALSE

-- The chapter does not prohibit a transaction conducted in accordance with Chapter 12A of Title 6 (Title 6, not among
-- the inputs) so long as the parts governed by this chapter are documented, signed and delivered in accordance with
-- this subsection or otherwise in accordance with this chapter. This subsection applies solely for deciding whether an
-- act or transaction has been documented, signed and delivered in accordance with this chapter, the certificate and
-- the bylaws.
-- src:228 | This chapter shall not prohibit 1 or more persons from conducting a transaction in accordance with Chapter 12A of Title 6 so long as the part or parts of the transaction that are governed by this chapter are documented, signed and delivered in accordance with this subsection or otherwise in accordance with this chapter. This subsection shall apply solely for purposes of determining whether an act or transaction has been documented, and the document has been signed and delivered, in accordance with this chapter, the certificate of incorporation and the bylaws.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(a) (src:228)
GIVEN `the parts of the transaction governed by this chapter are documented, signed and delivered in accordance with this subsection or otherwise in accordance with this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 116(a) this chapter does not prohibit conducting the transaction in accordance with Chapter 12A of Title 6` `the parts of the transaction governed by this chapter are documented, signed and delivered in accordance with this subsection or otherwise in accordance with this chapter` MEANS
    -- out of range: Chapter 12A of Title 6
    `the parts of the transaction governed by this chapter are documented, signed and delivered in accordance with this subsection or otherwise in accordance with this chapter`

§§ `s 116(b) What subsection (a) does not apply to`

-- src:229 | (b) Subsection (a) of this section shall not apply to:
-- src:230 | (1) A document filed with or submitted to the Secretary of State, the Register in Chancery, or a court or other judicial or governmental body of this State;
-- src:231 | (2) A document comprising part of the stock ledger;
-- src:232 | (3) A certificate representing a security;
-- src:233 | (4) Any document expressly referenced as a notice (or waiver of notice) by this chapter, the certificate of incorporation or bylaws;
-- src:234 | (5) [Repealed.]
-- src:235 | (6) A ballot to vote on actions at a meeting of stockholders; and
-- src:236 | (7) An act or transaction effected pursuant to § 280 of this title or subchapters III, XIII or XVI of this chapter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(b) (src:229-236)
DECLARE `s 116(b) Kind of document` IS ONE OF
    `a document filed with or submitted to the Secretary of State, the Register in Chancery, or a court or other judicial or governmental body of this State`
    `a document comprising part of the stock ledger`
    `a certificate representing a security`
    `any document expressly referenced as a notice (or waiver of notice) by this chapter, the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws`
    `a ballot to vote on actions at a meeting of stockholders`
    `an act or transaction effected pursuant to § 280 of this title or subchapters III, XIII or XVI of this chapter`
    `any other document`

-- Subsection (a) does not apply to the six kinds the text lists (paragraph (5) is repealed); it applies to any other
-- document.
-- src:229 | (b) Subsection (a) of this section shall not apply to:
-- src:230 | (1) A document filed with or submitted to the Secretary of State, the Register in Chancery, or a court or other judicial or governmental body of this State;
-- src:231 | (2) A document comprising part of the stock ledger;
-- src:232 | (3) A certificate representing a security;
-- src:233 | (4) Any document expressly referenced as a notice (or waiver of notice) by this chapter, the certificate of incorporation or bylaws;
-- src:235 | (6) A ballot to vote on actions at a meeting of stockholders; and
-- src:236 | (7) An act or transaction effected pursuant to § 280 of this title or subchapters III, XIII or XVI of this chapter.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(b) (src:229-233) (src:235-236)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 116(b) Kind of document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 116(b) subsection (a) applies to the document` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a document filed with or submitted to the Secretary of State, the Register in Chancery, or a court or other judicial or governmental body of this State` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a document comprising part of the stock ledger` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a certificate representing a security` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `any document expressly referenced as a notice (or waiver of notice) by this chapter, the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a ballot to vote on actions at a meeting of stockholders` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an act or transaction effected pursuant to § 280 of this title or subchapters III, XIII or XVI of this chapter` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `any other document` THEN TRUE

-- The exclusions create no presumption about the lawful means to document a matter they address, or the lawful means
-- to sign or deliver a document they address.
-- src:237 | The foregoing shall not create any presumption about the lawful means to document a matter addressed by this subsection, or the lawful means to sign or deliver a document addressed by this subsection. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(b) (src:237)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 116(b) a presumption arises from the exclusions about the lawful means to document, sign or deliver` MEANS FALSE

-- No provision of the certificate or the bylaws limits the application of subsection (a), except a provision that
-- expressly restricts or prohibits the use of an electronic transmission or electronic signature (or any form of
-- them) or expressly restricts or prohibits the delivery of an electronic transmission to an information processing
-- system.
-- src:237 | No provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaws shall limit the application of subsection (a) of this section except for a provision that expressly restricts or prohibits the use of an electronic transmission or electronic signature (or any form thereof) or expressly restricts or prohibits the delivery of an electronic transmission to an information processing system.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(b) (src:237)
GIVEN `the provision expressly restricts or prohibits the use of an electronic transmission or electronic signature, or any form of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision expressly restricts or prohibits the delivery of an electronic transmission to an information processing system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 116(b) the provision of the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws limits the application of subsection (a)` `the provision expressly restricts or prohibits the use of an electronic transmission or electronic signature, or any form of them` `the provision expressly restricts or prohibits the delivery of an electronic transmission to an information processing system` MEANS
        `the provision expressly restricts or prohibits the use of an electronic transmission or electronic signature, or any form of them`
     OR `the provision expressly restricts or prohibits the delivery of an electronic transmission to an information processing system`

§§ `s 116(c) The Electronic Signatures in Global and National Commerce Act`

-- If any provision of this chapter is deemed to modify, limit or supersede that Act (15 U.S.C. § 7001 et seq., federal
-- law, an input), the chapter controls to the fullest extent permitted by section 7002(a)(2) of the Act. If no
-- provision is so deemed there is nothing for the chapter to control (NOTHING).
-- src:238 | (c) In the event that any provision of this chapter is deemed to modify, limit or supersede the Electronic Signatures in Global and National Commerce Act, (15 U.S.C. § 7001 et. seq.), the provisions of this chapter shall control to the fullest extent permitted by § 7002(a)(2) of such act [15 U.S.C. § 7002(a)(2)].
@ref 8 Del. C. § 116(c) (src:238)
GIVEN `a provision of this chapter is deemed to modify, limit or supersede the Electronic Signatures in Global and National Commerce Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `controlling is permitted by § 7002(a)(2) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(c) this chapter controls` `a provision of this chapter is deemed to modify, limit or supersede the Electronic Signatures in Global and National Commerce Act` `controlling is permitted by § 7002(a)(2) of that Act` MEANS
    IF `a provision of this chapter is deemed to modify, limit or supersede the Electronic Signatures in Global and National Commerce Act`
    THEN JUST `controlling is permitted by § 7002(a)(2) of that Act`
    ELSE NOTHING
